Description: manage drives, network shares and /etc/fstab on KDE Plasma
 Anchorage is a KDE Plasma application for the places a computer mounts:
 internal and USB drives, folders shown in a second place (bind mounts),
 and SMB and NFS network shares. It edits /etc/fstab for you, explains
 each option in plain words, checks every change before saving it, and
 keeps a backup of the file before each change.
 .
 Changes to system files are made by a small helper that runs as root
 through polkit. Members of the "driveadmins" group can manage everything
 with their own password; members of "netmount" can add network shares.
 The package creates both groups but adds nobody to them.
